#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

"""Set up (or check) the sandbox the user-service port is developed in (ADR 0028).

The sandbox image provides Python, uv, Java, Node, git, the PostgreSQL 16
binaries, and bwrap, unshare and nsenter with unprivileged user namespaces
(tools/gluon-kube, ADR 0030); this script verifies those and installs everything the spike added on
top, without root, into the home directory. It is idempotent: run it after a
teardown, or any time, and it only installs what is missing. Every tool the
spike adds to the sandbox is added here in the same change (plans/private/sandbox.md).

Usage:
  bin/sandbox-setup            install what is missing, then report
  bin/sandbox-setup --check    report only; exit 1 if anything is missing
  bin/sandbox-setup --only rust vim
                               limit to the named steps

Steps: network, image, rust, node, cdc, vim, shellcheck, redis, shell, git-init, git-identity,
projects, browsers. Each uses what the sandbox already provides (on the PATH, a mirror)
and installs its own copy only when that is missing.
"""

import argparse
import json
import os
import platform
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
